  "_rawDocuments_maintained_by": "Raw JSON text, not a document to re-serialize: these vectors exist because encoding/json folds member names and keeps the last match while JSON.parse keeps every spelling, so the twin only survives in the bytes. Go passes the string to ValidateRules and TypeScript to validatePaymentRequestJSON, so both readers see identical bytes. wantErrKind is 'ambiguous' (refused before the rule runs), 'unsupported' (the rule refused it) or '' (admitted).",
